# HTTP Clients (Node.js)

## Options

- **Native fetch:** Built-in in Node 18+; use for simple requests
- **Undici:** Fast, low-level; use for high throughput or when fetch is insufficient
- **Axios:** Interceptors, request/response transform; good for APIs with consistent error shape

## Conventions

- **Base URL:** From env; never hardcode
- **Timeouts:** Set request timeout; handle ECONNABORTED
- **Errors:** Map HTTP status to domain errors; retry only on 5xx or network errors with backoff (see resilience.mdc)
- **Types:** Type response body (e.g. generic on client method); validate with Zod if API is untrusted
- **Headers:** Set Accept, Content-Type; add auth (Bearer, API key) per service

## Retries

- Use resilience pattern (retry with backoff, circuit breaker) for external calls; do not retry 4xx (except 429 with backoff)

## Conventions

- Single client instance per target (reuse connection); timeout and retry; type and validate responses; log errors with context (no secrets)

## Anti-Patterns

- No timeout; retrying 4xx; logging full response bodies; creating new client per request

**See also:** `resilience.mdc`, `error-handling.mdc`
